#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116243} :activity/id #uuid "ab69be82-a737-5ca5-bd57-46d2a37c64bb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050680 :topic/id #uuid "5e676adf-aa45-5e67-b4e5-57ec40661f6e" :topic/math-academy-id 1576} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116243 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116417 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find all of the values of $x$ that satisfy *either* $4x+2 < 6$ *or*\n\n$$\n2x \\geq 8\n$$\n\nTo do this, we solve each inequality individually and then compute the union of the two solutions.\n\nWe start by solving $4x+2 < 6$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4x + 2 & < 6 \\\\ 4x & < 4 \\\\ x & < 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/0d/0d36b8e68d9fd0b33b255502860481eeb525b60382029b17434bfb072cc39da2.png)\n\nThen, we solve\n\n$$\n2x \\geq 8\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x & \\ge 8 \\\\ x & \\ge 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n![](images/ed/edf5665b7cab7f51e3f252601a96d43c6f0cbfc64e5c9b8da81f0ef09d7b2f5a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/5c/5c60839a626f2ba8a0fe4a24f4011af0fa52c00d79fbf80039bcfdbdf0a612c7.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x < 1$ or\n\n$$\nx \\geq 4\n$$\n\nWe can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\n(-\\infty, 1) \\cup [4,\\infty)\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6d186c13-c1df-52d0-8ed6-a383185138a9" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1428 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "cdc53761-47a4-5dc1-a8a0-b21a01b5b35a" :step/math-academy-id 3201 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116245}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116244 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115321 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115153 :question/id #uuid "abae2e99-53b7-5d81-860c-9555ce50ec3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-965"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdaed02f-09f2-5572-a70c-0e6979ef2167" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115903} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115905}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving For the Union of Two Opposite-Sided Linear Inequalities that Overlap"} :step/id #uuid "eef16282-4281-509e-8f6c-106a707fcb20" :step/math-academy-id 3202 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116246}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116245 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115322 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115154 :question/id #uuid "81405a9f-882c-50fb-8057-41bb54515d14" :question/math-academy-id "e-966"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91a5169c-6a92-535d-85e1-8b9363b49274" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049986} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050229}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115575} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115577}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities"} :step/id #uuid "a370cd83-ae02-58f0-b487-2c4e2f90db1d" :step/math-academy-id 3205 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116244}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116246 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115155 :question/id #uuid "dced871e-e24d-5d06-a4bb-9faa933ecac7" :question/math-academy-id "e-967"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e3a4ead-02d0-5023-a7a7-3aaaca19b563" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050734}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115576} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115906}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Union of Two Linear Inequalities When One Inequality is Compound"} :step/id #uuid "634432ad-9cd7-5544-b7bb-1b5664235ef4" :step/math-academy-id 3208}] :activity/title "Compound OR Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186115415}]}
